      "LOUISE: Just fill it up with no lead.\nTHELMA: Where's a good restaurant around hEtre?\nLOUISE: We'll eat when we get to the cabin.\nTHELMA: How much longer is that gonna be?",
      "THELMA: Can't we go? Just for a few minutes?\nLOUISE: We're not gonna get to the cacin till after dark as it is, Thelma.\nTHELMA: Then what difference does it make if we stop? Come on. I never get to do stuff like this.\nLOUISE: Alright, but I really don't want to stay long.",
      "LOUISE: I haven't seen a place like this since I left Texas.\nTHELMA: Idn't this fun?",
      "THELMA: Louise ••• Are you alright?\nLOUISE: Oh Christ. Thelma.\nLOUISE: I've gotta stop for a minute. I've got to get it together. I just got to take a break. Now, I'm going in there. I'm gonna get a cup of coffe…\nLOUISE: Is t·hat yes? Are you up to this?",
      "LOUISE: We gotta be inconspicuous. Do you know what that means?\nTHELMA: Yes.\nLOUISE: It means you don't talk to anybody. You don't draw attention to yourself in any way. Do you understand that?\nLOUISE: Tell me you understand that."
    ]
